    "closure": "proof",
    "statement": "The calibrated kernel lifts admit one explicit common-denominator clearing F(z;X) of bidegree at most (2e,4e+6). At every active outside row, F(z;x)=(A(x)B(x))^2H_x(z). Therefore at each external slope gamma, F(gamma;X) is the exact degree-(4e+2) nonincidence locator times a unique nonzero polynomial of degree at most four. After known scalar normalization all such quartics are fibers of one biform Omega of bidegree at most (e-2,4), through FQ=(AB)^2q_eP_Z+CzI^2Omega. The e=1 exact Hankel fixture attains degree four and its cofactors are not base-field split, so the Omega-curve is not asserted to be a line.",
